MagBridge-Battery v1.0 — Upstream OSF Source Notice
=====================================================

This repository's bridge implementation incorporates aggregate statistical
artifacts derived from the Mohammadi–Jerschow OSF battery magnetometry
archive:

    Mohammadi, M. and Jerschow, A. "Battery Magnetometry Data 2019–2020."
    Open Science Framework, 2020. DOI: 10.17605/OSF.IO/CW8ZV.
    https://osf.io/cw8zv/

Associated peer-reviewed paper:

    Hu, Y., Iwata, G. Z., Mohammadi, M., Silletta, E. V., Wickenbrock, A.,
    Blanchard, J. W., Budker, D., and Jerschow, A. "Sensitive magnetometry
    reveals inhomogeneities in charge storage and weak transient internal
    currents in Li-ion cells." PNAS 117(20): 10667–10672, 2020.
    DOI: 10.1073/pnas.1917172117.


WHAT IS DERIVED FROM OSF IN THIS REPOSITORY
--------------------------------------------

The files at code/bridge/data/v1.0/ contain *derived* statistical artifacts
from the OSF archive, not raw OSF signal data:

    - anchor_stats.npz     Per-voltage-anchor mean trajectories and
                           per-channel variances, computed across the 41
                           OSF scan positions at each of the 5 voltage
                           anchors. Compresses 205 raw OSF samples into
                           per-anchor aggregates.

    - lda_fit.npz          Fitted Linear Discriminant Analysis model
                           parameters (means, covariances, projection
                           weights), trained on OSF samples with voltage
                           anchors as class labels.

    - qrec_embeddings.npz  171-dimensional MagBridge-Embed (quantum
                           reservoir) embeddings of the 205 OSF samples.
                           Each embedding compresses the raw length-100
                           six-channel signal to a 171-D vector.

These artifacts cannot be inverted back to the raw OSF signals.


RAW UPSTREAM FILES ARE NOT REDISTRIBUTED
-----------------------------------------

The raw OSF magnetic-scan files (per-sample signal sequences and sample
metadata) are NOT included in this repository. Users who wish to regenerate
the MagBridge-Battery dataset from scratch, or who need raw OSF signals for
their own work, should obtain the raw files directly from the OSF archive:

    https://osf.io/cw8zv/

and cite the original authors per the citations above.


